From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] input: edt-ft5x06: keep resume power-up symmetric when power is retained

Patch 0019 reworked this resume path so the re-initialization always
runs, and in doing so narrowed the early-return guard from

	if (device_may_wakeup(dev) || tsdata->retain_power_in_suspend)

down to

	if (device_may_wakeup(dev))

That change only guarded one half of the power cycle. When a board sets
edt,retain-power-in-suspend, edt_ft5x06_ts_suspend() still returns early
and never calls regulator_disable(), but the resume path went on to
toggle the reset line and call regulator_enable() on both vcc and iovcc
unconditionally. Every suspend/resume cycle therefore leaked one enable
reference per regulator.

The leak is silent until the controller is unbound, at which point the
devm cleanup action disables each regulator exactly once and
_regulator_put() trips WARN_ON(regulator->enable_count):

WARNING: drivers/regulator/core.c:2663 at _regulator_put+0x5c/0x70

On the AYN Thor both touch controllers are set edt,retain-power-in-suspend
(qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts), so 51-thorch-touchscreen-reprobe tripped this
twice per resume, once per controller, on every cycle. regulator_summary
showed the count climbing with the cycle count.

Restore the symmetry: when power was retained through suspend, skip the
reset toggle and the regulator_enable() calls and go straight to the
re-initialization. The re-initialization is what actually clears the
corrupted touch engine on resume, so it still runs unconditionally and
the fix from 0019 is preserved.

Fixes: 0019-input-edt-ft5x06-reinit-on-resume.patch
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -1457,36 +1457,49 @@
 			disable_irq(tsdata->client->irq);
 
 		/*
-		 * We can't check if the regulator is a dummy or a real
-		 * regulator. So we need to specify the 5ms reset time (T_rst)
-		 * here instead of the 100us T_rtp time. We also need to wait
-		 * 300ms in case it was a real supply and the power was cutted
-		 * of. Toggle the reset pin is also a way to exit the hibernate
-		 * mode.
+		 * Keep the power-up side symmetric with the power-down side.
+		 * edt_ft5x06_ts_suspend() returns early when power is
+		 * retained, so it never dropped these regulators. Toggling
+		 * the reset line and calling regulator_enable() here anyway
+		 * would leak one enable reference per suspend/resume cycle
+		 * and eventually trip WARN_ON(regulator->enable_count) in
+		 * _regulator_put() when the controller is unbound. Skip
+		 * straight to the re-initialization below, which is what
+		 * actually clears the corrupted touch engine.
 		 */
-		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(reset_gpio, 1);
-		usleep_range(5000, 6000);
-
-		ret = regulator_enable(tsdata->iovcc);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable iovcc\n");
-			return ret;
+		if (!tsdata->retain_power_in_suspend) {
+			/*
+			 * We can't check if the regulator is a dummy or a real
+			 * regulator. So we need to specify the 5ms reset time (T_rst)
+			 * here instead of the 100us T_rtp time. We also need to wait
+			 * 300ms in case it was a real supply and the power was cutted
+			 * of. Toggle the reset pin is also a way to exit the hibernate
+			 * mode.
+			 */
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(reset_gpio, 1);
+			usleep_range(5000, 6000);
+
+			ret = regulator_enable(tsdata->iovcc);
+			if (ret) {
+				dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable iovcc\n");
+				return ret;
+			}
+
+			/* Delay enabling VCC for > 10us (T_ivd) after IOVCC */
+			usleep_range(10, 100);
+
+			ret = regulator_enable(tsdata->vcc);
+			if (ret) {
+				dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable vcc\n");
+				regulator_disable(tsdata->iovcc);
+				return ret;
+			}
+
+			usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(reset_gpio, 0);
+			msleep(300);
 		}
 
-		/* Delay enabling VCC for > 10us (T_ivd) after IOVCC */
-		usleep_range(10, 100);
-
-		ret = regulator_enable(tsdata->vcc);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable vcc\n");
-			regulator_disable(tsdata->iovcc);
-			return ret;
-		}
-
-		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
-		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(reset_gpio, 0);
-		msleep(300);
-
 		/*
 		 * Re-run the probe-time initialization.  The FT5x06
 		 * controllers on some boards (AYN Thor) come back from s2idle
